# Fetched CC0/OFL assets — regenerate with `npx tsx scripts/fetchAssets.ts`
public/assets/

# THIRD-PARTY ARTWORK. Issue #36.
#
# `src/render/BrandAssets.ts` resolves `public/brand/<team-id>/<slot>.png|webp|svg`
# for the team badge, the sponsor decal, the driver portrait and a replacement
# livery, plus `public/brand/shared/` for materials, LUTs and environment maps.
# Drop a file in and it appears on the next reload; take it away and the game
# falls back to the generated marks in `LiveryDesign.ts` and `Livery.ts`.
#
# NOT THE SAME THING AS `public/assets/` ABOVE, and the difference is the
# licence. That directory is FETCHED — CC0/OFL only, by a script, with the
# licence of every file written down beside it, and it is regenerable from a
# clean clone. This one is a DROP BOX: whatever the user wants on their own
# machine while testing, licensed or not, with no manifest and no promises.
#
# IT IS IGNORED BECAUSE THAT IS THE ENTIRE POINT OF THE SLOT. The repo has to
# stay shippable while the user tests locally with whatever artwork they like,
# and a badge or a livery committed here by accident is the one thing that would
# make it not. `npm run probe:assets` proves that deleting this directory
# returns the render to byte-identical.
public/brand/

# Side-by-side comparisons written by `npm run probe:grade`. Evidence, not build.
grade-out/

# Agent scratch: parameter sweeps and one-off fits. Never part of a build.
scratch/

# The symlink an agent worktree makes to the main checkout.
/public/assets
